# Test output and local env.
#
# Every `.env` variant, matching `.gitignore` — the Dockerfile does `COPY . .`,
# so a variant named outside the two the previous list knew about would be
# baked into an image layer and survive every later `rm`.
test-results
playwright-report
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Docs are not needed in the build context
*.md
!README.md

# Python build and cache artefacts. The Python image copies `packages/sdk-python`
# wholesale for the editable path dependency, so a local `__pycache__` or `.venv`
# would ride into the image — stale bytecode compiled against a different
# interpreter, and a virtualenv holding absolute host paths.
#
# `**/` on every one of them: .dockerignore is not .gitignore. A bare
# `__pycache__/` is matched against the whole relative path, so it excludes only
# a directory at the context root — `packages/sdk-python/portal_sdk/__pycache__`
# would sail straight through it.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/

# .NET build output. The hub image does COPY . ., so without these a local
# dotnet build rides into it — and obj/ holds absolute host paths.
#
# Scoped to the package that produces them, for the same reason the .gitignore
# rule is: `bin/` is an ordinary name for a committed script directory, and an
# unscoped `**/bin/` silently drops one from the build context, where the
# failure shows up as a missing file at runtime rather than at build time.
#
# Every .NET project needs its own pair, and forgetting one is quiet: the
# satellite image does `COPY ${APP_PATH}`, and `scripts/verify-ci.sh` runs
# `dotnet test` in `apps/satellite-depots` on the way to the build — so the
# obj/ it leaves behind, full of absolute host paths, would ride into the
# image on the very next `pnpm up`.
packages/sdk-csharp/**/bin/
packages/sdk-csharp/**/obj/
apps/satellite-depots/**/bin/
apps/satellite-depots/**/obj/
